# Expo environment variables for @forge/tv
# ------------------------------------------
# Local dev: pull secrets from Doppler
#   pnpm fetch-secrets
#   (writes to .env.local — highest priority, gitignored)
#
# EAS builds: env vars come from EAS Environments (expo.dev dashboard)
#   Preview -> "preview" environment
#
# Note: only the `preview` profile is in scope today (see plan).
# A `production` profile + EAS Environment will be added if/when the TV app
# graduates from internal-stakeholder distribution.

# ── GraphQL endpoint (required) ──────────────────────────────────────
# TV apps run on a single screen factor; no per-platform split needed.
# Local dev points at host Strapi (Apple TV simulator and Android TV
# emulator both reach host via the host machine's network IP, not
# 10.0.2.2/localhost — confirm the IP your network exposes).
EXPO_PUBLIC_GRAPHQL_URL=http://192.168.1.1:1337/graphql

# ── Strapi API token (optional for local dev) ────────────────────────
# Required if Strapi restricts public read access on the preview endpoint.
# In EAS builds, set via EAS Environments (visibility: sensitive).
# Token MUST be read-only — EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the JS
# bundle and extractable from any installed binary.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_STRAPI_TOKEN=
